## Do's and Don'ts

### Do

- Pass `text` as the plain-text version of your content (always required)
- Use `children` for rich content with interactive elements
- Use `<EtText onPress>` for inline interactive text within children
- Use `onLinkPress` for auto-detecting URLs in string mode
- Use `customActionComponent` for custom icons or complex actions
- Use `maxLines` to control the visible text amount
- Use `onExpandedChange` to track analytics or sync state

### Don't

- Don't use `<EtLink>` inside children — it's View-based and can't be nested in Text
- Don't use for short text that won't need truncation (no visual effect)
- Don't hardcode colors — the component uses theme colors automatically
- Don't forget to pass `text` when using children (needed for measurement)
- Don't use `onLinkPress` with children (handle links in children's onPress instead)
